      "writtenOn": "2026-08-20T18:55:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "When I looked at `CancellableDigestOutputStream`, it seemed it should already handle this, but that only happens if 1) there\u0027s a ProgressMonitor that isn\u0027t `NullProgressMonitor.INSTANCE` and 2) that progress monitor reports `isCancelled() \u003d\u003d true` when interrupted. AFAICT, all of the `ProgressMonitor` implementations always return `false`.\n\nMaybe instead of updating WindowCursor and ObjectDirectory, update the ProgressMonitor interface to have a default `isCancelled()` that checks if the thread is interrupted (and remove the hardcoded `return false` in implementors)?",
      "revId": "91b1ccbb97c77b06ebb290ba20c6086ec9108334",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
